        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Question Three\n",
        "The prime factors of $13195$ are $5, 7, 13$ and $29$\n",
        "What is the largest prime factor of the number $600851475143$?\n",
        "\n",
        "Prime factorization is one of the great modern questions of math and computer science. One relatively quick way of finding prime factors for a number is called the [Sieve Of Ersatosthenes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sieve_of_Eratosthenes)\n",
        "\n",
        "Implementing the Sieve is a kind of a dynamic programming solution, we need to list a lot of numbers and eliminate them as we go.\n",
        "\n",
        "This time I am going to benchmark python loops against cpp loops against r loops. I am going to use a few tricks, like only doing odd numbers\n"
      ],
      "id": "16fd9aac"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "n = 600851475143\n",
        "def sieve(n):\n",
        "    candidate_nums = list(range(3, n // 2 + 1, 2))\n",
        "    num_len = len(candidate_nums)\n",
        "    is_valid = [TRUE] * num_len\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for i in 1:num_len:\n",
        "        test_num = candidate_nums[i]\n"
      ],
      "id": "4d2b59e8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
